## What the tests check

Four cases in `free_space_test`, listed in step A4. Step B has **no test of its own**.

## Gaps found

| What | Where |
|---|---|
| **Two door sizes.** Step A cuts a room at a gap narrower than 1.0 m (twice `door_radius`). Step B closes a gap up to 1.2 m (`door_max`). The two settings are not linked: a door of 1.1 m is not a cut in step A, but is closed in step B | `free_space.cpp`, `rooms.cpp` |
| The [Domain](domain.qd) says a doorway can leave a room open. In the code a gap up to `door_max` is **closed**, so a door never makes a room open | `rooms.cpp` |
| The room outline is the **box** around the flood, so an L-shaped room gets an outline that is too big (a TODO) | `rooms.cpp` |
| Step A has a TODO: it cannot tell a closed room from one still open toward floor not seen yet | `free_space.cpp` |
| Step A starts over on every run, so the room numbers of the free floor can change between two runs on a growing map | `free_space.hpp` |
| **No path, no room.** With no poses, step A returns nothing, so there are no walls either | `free_space.cpp` |
| Step B has no test | `backend/tests/` |
